In git, a branch is a new / seperate version of the main repository.

branches allow you to work on different parts of a project without impacting main branch.when the work is completed a branch can be mergrd with main branch

# making a new branch 

git branch -c " new branch name" _OR_ git branch <name of the branch>

# list the branches 

 git branch -a OR git branch

 # switching to new branch 
  
  git checkout <branch name > OR  git switch <branch name> (switching the branches)

 # deleting branch 
  
  git branch -d <branch name> (deletes the branch>

 #making a new branch and switching to new brach
 
 git checkout -b < branch name > ( this lets you createnew branch and switch to it ) -b is branch

 # merging branch 
 
   to merge the branch you have to be be in the main branch and run the command 

   git merge <branch name>

